cf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.046515113834492715,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":46.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03034280209695498,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.08439392364503684,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00068999996,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Corporaci\u00f3n Inmobiliaria Vesta, S.A.B. de C.V., together with its subsidiaries, acquires, develops, manages, operates industrial buildings and distribution facilities in Mexico. It offers rental income from operating leases, including reimbursable building services and energy income. The company serves corporations in diverse industries, such as food and beverage, automotive, aerospace, medical, logistics, and plastics. Corporaci\u00f3n Inmobiliaria Vesta, S.A.B. de C.V. was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in Mexico City, Mexico.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lorenzo Dominique Berho Carranza | CEO & Alternate Director | Age 42","financial_summary":["Corporacion Inmobiliaria Vesta, is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.5B market cap on $283M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are contracting by -48.5pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $206M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 73 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.86\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 5.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -48.5pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4806693594922071},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thes